{"step_index":63,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-16T22:04:29Z","model":"gemini-4-argon-high","input_tokens":2403,"cache_read_tokens":74471,"output_tokens":799,"content":"The Python `counting_sort` program has been formalized in Lean 4 at [counting_sort.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/counting_sort.lean).\n\n### Summary of Formalization\n\n1. **Functional Implementation** ([counting_sort.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/counting_sort.lean#L24-L42)):\n   - `countStep` and `counting_sort` faithfully translate the Python algorithm over `List Int`: returning `[]` on empty input, computing `max_val` and `min_val`, shifting indices by `min_val` into a frequency table of size `range_size = (max_val - min_val + 1).toNat`, and reconstructing the sorted list from the frequency counts.\n2. **Unit Tests** ([counting_sort.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/counting_sort.lean#L44-L93)):\n   - `example : ... := by native_decide` and `#eval` tests covering all cases from the Python `check` suite as well as negative-number shift cases.\n3. **Pre-condition, Properties, and Proofs** ([counting_sort.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/counting_sort.lean#L95-L506)):\n   - `Pre` (`True` on statically typed `List Int`) and 20 property definitions (`_prop`) paired with kernel-checked theorems (`_thm`), all proved without `sorry`, `admit`, `native_decide`, or extra axioms:\n     - `empty_thm`, `empty_iff_thm`, `singleton_thm`\n     - `count_thm` (multiplicity preservation), `perm_thm` (`List.Perm`), `length_thm`, `mem_thm`\n     - `sorted_thm` (`List.Sorted (· ≤ ·)`), `chain_sorted_thm` (`List.Chain' (· ≤ ·)`), `index_sorted_thm`\n     - `bounds_thm`, `head_min_thm`, `getLast_max_thm`\n     - `already_sorted_thm`, `idempotent_thm`, `perm_invariant_thm`, `reverse_thm`, `replicate_thm`, `shift_thm`, `eq_mergeSort_thm`\n4. **Post-condition, Property-Based Tests, and Main Correctness Theorem** ([counting_sort.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/counting_sort.lean#L508-L629)):\n   - `Post_prop` combining the specification properties of `counting_sort`.\n   - Randomized `Plausible.Testable.check` PBTs and bounded `native_decide` PBTs covering each property and `Post_prop`.\n   - `counting_sort_correct` / `correctness_thm` proving `Pre arr → Post_prop arr`.\n5. **Imperative Implementation and Equivalence Proof** ([counting_sort.lean](file:///home/user/lean_project/Veribench/counting_sort.lean#L631-L699)):\n   - `counting_sort_imp` implemented with `Id.run do` and mutable state (`max_val`, `min_val`, `count`, `result`), imperative unit/PBT checks, and the proved equivalence theorem `equiv_thm` (`counting_sort arr = counting_sort_imp arr`)."}
